# phi-agent — local, non-repository configuration.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/phi-agent/env and edit. phi-agent-contain SOURCES this
# file as a shell fragment: one `KEY=value` per line, no `export`, no logic —
# but shell rules apply, so quote any value that contains a space
# ("like this") and `$HOME` / `~` expand.
#
# NOTHING SECRET GOES HERE. The provider API key is held by the brokering
# service outside the containment and is read from its own file (S-71); the
# remote-surface password is a systemd credential from a root-owned file
# (S-74). This file only carries paths and identity.

# --- A1 (assistant) ---
#
# There is NO system-level "notes folder" any more (phios-agente-delta.md
# D-03). Notes are an ordinary project: `phi agent project new notes
# --folder ~/Notes --personality notes`, then `phi agent project use notes`.
# A project's folders of interest are read-only and live in its own
# project.json / folders.list.

# The active project. Normally written by `phi agent project use <name>`, not
# by hand. Leave unset to start A1 with no project (valid for the V-01..V-04
# proof and for `phi agent ask`).
#PHI_AGENT_PROJECT=

# --- A2 (worker) ---
#
# There is NO fixed "code root" any more (phios-agente-delta.md D-03). Open
# the coding agent in any directory: `phi agent code ~/dev/some-project`.
# That directory is the ONLY thing under $HOME the session can see. A
# configurable blocklist (~/.config/phi-agent/code-blocklist, copy it from
# code-blocklist.example) guards the picker; it is not the security boundary.

# Toolchain caches dedicated to A2, kept separate from your own (§4.4).
#PHI_AGENT_A2_TOOLCHAIN_CACHE=$HOME/.cache/phi-agent/a2/toolchains

# Git identity for A2's local commits. A2 never mounts your ~/.gitconfig.
# Quoted: the value has a space (see the sourcing note at the top).
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="phi agent"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=phi-agent@localhost

# --- A2 remote surface (only if you use it — S-74, §10.3) ---

# The overlay (Tailscale) address of THIS machine, literal, no shell
# expansion — this is the only interface phi-agent-a2-remote.service will
# bind. Machine data: it belongs here, never in the repository (ADR 067).
# The unit refuses to start while this is unset.
#PHI_AGENT_REMOTE_ADDR=

# The single directory a REMOTE A2 session opens (delta D-03: there is no
# code root). A literal absolute path — systemd's EnvironmentFile parser does
# not expand ~ or $HOME. The remote-engine unit refuses to start while unset.
#PHI_AGENT_REMOTE_WORKDIR=/home/you/dev/the-project

# The remote-session auth password is NOT set here. Put the raw password in
# ~/.config/phi-agent/a2/remote-password (chmod 600); the unit loads it as
# a systemd credential.
